Photorealistic vintage 1968 vacuum-tube recording studio console asset: one single wide horizontal push button plate, viewed perfectly straight-on, centered, spanning 88 percent of image width and about one quarter of its height, isolated on a pure flat black background. Shape: long horizontal rectangular bar with softly rounded ends, inspired by Abbey Road and EMI mixing desks. Frame: solid hand-beaten warm brushed brass bezel with slotted aged brass screws at left and right ends. Face: dark oiled English walnut timber inlay with subtle wood grain, and a warm glowing amber-orange filament neon halo glowing just inside the brass bezel. Vintage British audiophile console hardware, jewelry-grade studio photography, crisp focus, symmetrical, warm directional studio lighting. Absolutely no text, no letters, no symbols, no icons. One object only, pure flat black background, no watermark.
